[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Housing/PropertyResource.cs" id="1_property"]

; The first holding: a cottage on the south edge of the Ember Crown's square. Gated on the guild's
; standing goblin bounty rather than sold outright — the town sells a house to someone who has done
; something for the town — and then priced on top, so the quest earns you the right to pay rather
; than replacing the payment. 600 gold is reachable but not incidental by the time that bounty is
; done; Phase 38 owns economy balance and this is the sink it will tune.

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_property")
Id = "property.ember_crown.cottage"
NameKey = "property.cottage.name"
RegionId = "region.ember_crown"
PriceGold = 600
RequiredQuestId = "quest.warband.bounty"
TravelNodeId = "travel.ember_crown.cottage"

; 37C/37D/37E — the yard you may build in. Re-centred by 37E when the holding moved out of the town
; square into its own cell.
;
; ⚠️ WORLD COORDINATES, AND THE CORRECTION IS NOW ON BOTH AXES. A point read out of a cell's .tscn is
; LOCAL; world = local + the cell's Center. The homestead's Center is (52, 0, 46), so the yard at
; local (6, 8) is world (58, 0, 54). Until 37E this cell was the town hub at (0, 0, -10) and the note
; here said "add -10 on z" — read that against the new cell and every prop lands 52 m west in a
; market square. The number to trust is the Center in data/regions/EmberCrown.tres, never this
; comment's arithmetic.
;
; ⚠️ THE BUILD YARD MOVED WITH THE PLOT (the 2026-08-28 layout rebuild). It was seven metres of ground south-east of the
; house at local (6, 8); the rebuild put the cottage in the plot's north-east corner and the workshop
; along the east wall, so that circle now sits half on top of the workshop row. It is the SOUTH LAWN
; instead: local (0, 5), world (52, 0, 51), a 7 m circle bounded by the south fence at z = 12 and
; clear of the cottage (which ends at local z = -1), the workshop (x = 14), the kitchen garden's
; dividing fence at x = -7.2, Veyra's shrine at (12, 4) and every stone of the approach path — a
; player who fences their own front drive in has to walk round it.
;
; ⚠️ WORLD COORDINATES. A point read out of a cell's .tscn is LOCAL; world = local + the cell's
; Center, which is (52, 0, 46) for this cell. The number to trust is the Center in
; data/regions/EmberCrown.tres, never a comment's arithmetic — an earlier note here said "add -10 on
; z" from when this holding was in the town square, and read against the new cell that lands every
; placed prop 52 m west in a market.
; ⚠️ MOVED WITH THE CELL (the 2026-08-29 geography overhaul). The homestead's Center went from
; (52, 0, 46) to (95, 0, 85) when the realm's lattice grew; the SOUTH LAWN is still cell-local
; (0, 5), which is world (95, 0, 90). Read the local offset, never the old world number — that is
; the third time this exact line has had to be corrected and the second time for the same reason.
PlacementCenter = Vector3(95, 0, 90)
PlacementRadius = 7.0
